Now the "构造性确定性" (constructive determinism) connection: CLAUDE.md EP free-running discipline says "every dummy-row input must be constructively deterministic". The PagePool's stack-discipline allocator is the memory-side analog: given the same schedule, the same page ids. And padding_page_id is fixed at construction (always page 0 in current construction order — but the API contract is just "reserved deterministically at construction"). Actually should I say "always 0"? Let me verify: KvPool::with_storage_and_format creates PagePool::new(num_pages), then try_acquire_many(1) → pops PageId(0). So yes, in current code padding_page_id() == 0 always. I can state this as an observable consequence, noting it follows from the construction order. That's a nice concrete detail. But is it a *guarantee* or an implementation detail? It's an implementation consequence; I'll present it as "当前实现下恒为 0" — accurate.

