For 4.1 core flow: pseudocode of try_acquire_many: check n==0 → empty permit; lock; if len < n → None (no partial); pop n pages; wrap in permit. All-or-nothing atomicity.

Math: maybe present the invariant: available + Σ permits' len == capacity_pages. That's a nice invariant formula using \( ... \). The conservation law: 任意时刻 \( \text{available\_pages} + \sum_{p \in \text{permits}} p.\text{len}() = \text{capacity\_pages} \). Good use of the required math format.

For 4.2 Drop flow: mem::take → lock → extend(rev). Explain why rev: 归还的页按被借出顺序重新位于栈顶，下一次按原顺序再次借出 —— 同一调度序列 ⇒ 同一页号分配（构造性确定性）。And full-release restores exact initial layout.

Also explain why `std::mem::take`: move pages out of &mut self before locking — actually it takes then locks; the reason to take is that `self.pages` needs to be moved into the free list while drop only has &mut. It also means the Vec's buffer is reused by into_iter... minor. The key: take leaves self.pages empty (idempotent drop safety), then lock and extend. Also note early return for empty pages avoids locking when nothing to return (zero-acquire permits drop cheaply — matters because KvPool::alloc hands out empty permits routinely).

For 4.3 absorb: Arc::ptr_eq assert; pages.append — O(1) splice (Vec::append moves elements, reusing allocation when capacity suffices... actually append moves all elements, potentially reallocating self.pages, but no per-element free-list ops). Key: absorb 不经过 free list —— 页从未"过池"，避免任何窗口被其他线程抢走；这正是 kv_pool 两段式准入 commit 半段的原子性来源。absorb(other) 之后 other 的 Drop 不再归还（已被 move）。When absorber drops, all pages (own + absorbed) return together, reversed as one batch.

try_grow: check-then-take under one lock hold; failure leaves permit unchanged (comment line 100). Used by ensure_capacity in decode loop when a request grows beyond its current pages (kv_pool.rs:360-374) — bail! with "out of pages" if grow fails.

Difference absorb vs try_grow: absorb 合并"已属于某个许可"的页；try_grow 从池里新借。And the kv_pool doc comment at L274-277: "Growing a request's own permit instead cannot be undone" — i.e., for multi-pool admission you must reserve-then-commit (absorb), because try_grow immediately takes and can't roll back. Great point from source: kv_pool.rs:274-277.

